<article class="env-corollary" id="039A">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/039A">Corollary <span data-tag="039A">7.1.5.22</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a cartesian fibration of $\infty $-categories. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
For each object $D \in \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$, the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{D} = \{ D\}  \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ has an initial object. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The functor $U$ is a coreflective localization: that is, it admits a fully faithful left adjoint $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Corollaries <a data-tag="0399" href="/tag/0399">7.1.5.15</a> and <a data-tag="02WV" href="/tag/02WV">7.1.5.21</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
